 "result_text": "I changed the default `dayfirst` in `parse()` from `True` to `False` (`delorean/interface.py:15`). With `yearfirst=True`, `dayfirst=True` made `2017-05-02` read as year-day-month, which is why you got February 5th. The default now reads it as year-month-day. Callers can still pass `dayfirst=True`.\n\nI couldn't confirm the fix end to end. Running your example now fails with `AttributeError: 'zoneinfo.ZoneInfo' object has no attribute 'localize'`. That comes from the timezone handling in `delorean/dates.py:157`, which expects a pytz timezone. The `Z` suffix gives a dateutil timezone, and I didn't change that code. The failure happens after the date has been parsed, so it doesn't show whether the date is now correct. `pytest -q tests` also ran no tests, so the existing suite hasn't been run against this change.",
